    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy are delighted to introduce No. 34 Tayleurs Point to the market, a well-maintained and beautifully proportioned two-bedroom home with the added benefit of a converted attic and second bathroom just mintues from the beach. This lovely property is ideally positioned within this popular and family-friendly development and offers comfortable and versatile living accommodation throughout. The property comprises two bedrooms, two bathrooms, a converted attic and a maintance free rear garden, providing excellent outdoor space. Boasting an energy-efficient B rating, this home ensures lower energy costs, and eligibility for favorable Green Mortgage interest rates. \n\nTayleurs Point is a highly sought-after residential development situated on the peninsula of Rush, with the coastline and beautiful seashore walks quite literally on the doorstep. The property is ideally located close to a host of local amenities and services including national and secondary schools, shops, restaurants and public transport.\n\nRush is a charming seaside village with an excellent selection of amenities and a strong community atmosphere. The property is conveniently located for neighbouring towns including Skerries and Lusk, while Dublin Airport and Dublin City Centre are easily accessible. The area is well serviced by both bus and rail transport, with Rush & Lusk train station just a short drive away, while the M1 motorway provides convenient access to Dublin and surrounding areas.\n\nNo. 34 offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a wonderful home in a desirable coastal location, with the added benefit of a converted attic and additional bathroom. Viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Converted Attic with Bathroom</li><li> Maintenance Free Private Garden</li><li> Double Glazed Windows Throughout</li><li> Minutes Walk to Beach and Rush Harbour</li><li> Family Friendly Location</li><li> Two Double Bedroom</li><li> Spacious Living Accommodation</li><li> Gas Fired Central Heating</li><li> B Rated Energy Efficient Home</ul>"
      },
